    <ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock id="f-350" contextRef="c-05">&lt;div class="Section_1"&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Tahoma"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 54pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-indent: -36pt; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Tahoma"&gt;1.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 7.82pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Tahoma"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 54pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-indent: -36pt; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Tahoma"&gt;2.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 7.82pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Tahoma"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 54pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-indent: -36pt; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Tahoma"&gt;3.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 7.82pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Tahoma"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 54pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-indent: -36pt; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Tahoma"&gt;4.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 7.82pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Tahoma"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 54pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-indent: -36pt; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Tahoma"&gt;5.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 7.82pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Tahoma"&gt;N/A&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 		&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock>
    <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-352" contextRef="c-05">&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="Section_1"&gt; 			&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: unset; font-size: 1em; font-weight: bold; text-align: inherit"&gt;The Company&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="Section_1"&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Texas Express Pipeline LLC (&amp;quot;Texas Express&amp;quot;) is a Delaware limited liability company.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Texas Express is owned 35% by Enterprise Products Operating LLC (EPOLLC), a Texas limited liability company, 35% by TEPCO Energy, LLC a Texas limited liability company, 20% by WES Texas Express Pipeline LLC, a Delaware limited liability company and 10% by DCP Partners Logistics, LLC, a Delaware limited liability company.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;EPOLLC is the operator of Texas Express.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;Description of the Property&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Texas Express is a 593 mile, 20&amp;quot; diameter natural gas liquids (&amp;quot;NGL&amp;quot;) pipeline located entirely within the State of Texas that provides pipeline transportation services for mixed NGLs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;The pipeline receives the NGLs at Skellytown, Texas and other receipt points on the trunkline.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Texas Express transports to delivery points in the Mont Belvieu, Texas area.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;Basis of Accounting&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The accounting policies followed in preparation of these financial statements conform to those required by FERC.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Financial statements are prepared on the accrual basis of accounting.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Texas Express property, plant and equipment assets are recorded at original cost.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;Revenue Recognition&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The revenues of Texas Express are derived from transportation of NGLs regulated by the FERC and the Railroad Commission of Texas.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Texas Express invoices shippers upon receipt of product into the pipeline, but recognizes revenues upon product delivery.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Revenues billed for product not yet delivered at balance sheet date are deferred until such time as product is actually delivered.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;During 2025, Texas Express rebilled shippers for under-recovery resulting from the vacated January 20, 2022 rehearing order (Docket No. RM20-14-001) in the amount of $7,361,457.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt; (See Commission's order issued on November 20, 2025 (Docket No. RM93-11-003, paragraph 37, footnote 111)).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;These revenues are reported in account 645 &amp;quot;Unusual or Infrequent Items (credit)&amp;quot; on page 114.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Texas Express is a limited liability company that passes income tax liability through the company to its members and does not, with the exception of the Texas Franchise Tax, recognize this liability on the company's financial statements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;For purposes of calculating the income tax expense and liability for the annual cost of service (shown on page 700 of the Annual Report) Texas Express employs FERC's Policy Statement on Income Tax Allowances.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: unset; font-size: 1em; text-align: inherit; font-weight: bold"&gt;Employees&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Texas Express has no employees of its own.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;All operations, management and administrative functions are performed by employees of Enterprise Products Company on behalf of EPOLLC, as operator.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Texas Express reimburses EPOLLC for management and administrative functions under the terms of an operating agreement.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 		&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
